## std.strerr (spec err.str.1-3, ADR 1129): the error type of `T ! str`.
## A function that declares `T ! str` fails with a `StrError`, an error whose
## text is the message it was made with. `return "bad input"` builds one; the
## loader (`compiler/load/strerr.ail`) writes the `StrError(why: ...)` for a
## string literal or interpolation, and a `str` held in a variable is wrapped
## by hand: `strerr.StrError(why: text)`. Printing the error prints `why`.

## The failure of a function declared `T ! str`.
pub error struct StrError "{self.why}"
    pub why str
